# The generator's type table (docs/RUNTIME.md section 3.2).  Planner-owned.
#
# Every parameter type and return type of a SHIM line must be a name in this file, or `T *`
# (any number of stars, const allowed) for a T in this file.  A name that is not here is a
# generator error, never a guess: a worker who needs one stops and reports.
#
#     <type name>   <class>   [size in bytes, for struct8 and struct]
#
# Classes, and how each crosses the Windows x64 ABI (section 3.1):
#     i8 u8 i16 u16     low bits of the argument's register or stack slot; the rest is undefined
#     i32 u32           low 32 bits; the upper half is undefined on entry and written as zero on return
#     i64 u64           the whole register or slot
#     ptr               a guest pointer (guest address == host address)
#     str wstr          a pointer to a NUL-terminated string the callee only reads; the call trace prints it
#     handle            a HANDLE of any kind
#     guestfn           a guest code address: call it with GUEST_CALL, never as a C function
#     f32 f64           xmm0-xmm3 chosen by position for arguments 0-3, a stack slot after that; returned in xmm0
#     struct8           a struct or union of 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes: by value in the register or slot
#     struct            any other struct: the argument is a pointer to the caller's copy (the thunk copies it
#                       for you); as a return type the caller passes the destination as a hidden argument 0
#     void              return type only, and the base of `void *`
#
# `const char *` and `const WCHAR *` are class str and wstr; every other `T *` is class ptr.
#
# FORBIDDEN in any shim signature and in any guest-visible type: long, unsigned long, wchar_t,
# size_t.  They differ between x64 Windows and arm64 macOS (section 3.3).
#
# The build checks that every name below exists and has the size its class says
# (build/gen/shim_types_check.c), so this file cannot drift from the headers.

@include rt/win/base.h
@include rt/win/memory.h
@include rt/win/sysinfo.h
